WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.850
Take Thomas Cole's The Oxbow from 1836.

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.700
The Connecticut River Valley splits
into wilderness

3
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.890
on one side and disciplined farmland
on the other.

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.670
It's a before-and-after shot
of civilization etched right into the landscape.

5
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.980
And yet the Algonquian peoples
who cultivated, hunted, burned,

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.330
and governed this valley
for centuries? Absent.

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.630
Even the one human figure, Cole himself,

8
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.460
is a tiny witness observing what the painting
treats as a natural,

9
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.290
almost inevitable transformation.
